IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P9-gate`

-- P9-art-88-94: Chapter IX Section 5 "Supervision, investigation, enforcement and monitoring in respect of providers of
-- general-purpose AI models": Articles 88 "Enforcement of the obligations of providers of general-purpose AI models",
-- 89 "Monitoring actions", 90 "Alerts of systemic risks by the scientific panel", 91 "Power to request documentation and
-- information", 92 "Power to conduct evaluations", 93 "Power to request measures" and 94 "Procedural rights of economic
-- operators of the general-purpose AI model" (consolidated text of 27.7.2026; unchanged by the Omnibus).
-- Group General (2 August 2026; Chapter IX is not in Article 113's third paragraph, point (b)). No AI system is in question
-- (the Section is about AI models): every function takes `the date asked`, and before the group applies the answer is NOTHING.
-- The Commission, the AI Office, the Board and the scientific panel are officials: no seat. What the Section means to the
-- provider of a general-purpose AI model (what may be requested of it, what it must supply, and by when) and to a downstream
-- provider (the right to complain) is asked in the seat modules.
-- "May" functions gated by "where", "when", "upon" or "after" are listed as split site (ii) in NOTES.md with the answer
-- the Guide's ruling (b) gives (JUST FALSE), one fork line each: F-88-2, F-90-1, F-90-2, F-91-3, F-92-1a, F-92-1b, F-93-1a, F-93-1b.
-- A "may" gated by "if" (Article 93(3)) answers NOTHING (the Guide's grant rule; the Guide's "if" line points the other way, so the site is marginal), fork F-93-3.
-- Seams: whether a model is a general-purpose AI model, or one with systemic risk (Articles 3(63), 51), is the caller's input.

§ `Article 88: enforcement of the obligations of providers of general-purpose AI models`

DECLARE `Art 88 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 88 the Commission`

DECLARE `Art 88 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 88(1) entrust the implementation of the tasks of supervising and enforcing Chapter V to the AI Office`

-- src:1369 | 1. The Commission shall have exclusive powers to supervise and enforce Chapter V, taking into account the procedural guarantees under Article 94. The Commission shall entrust the implementation of these tasks to the AI Office, without prejudice to the powers of organisation of the Commission and the division of competences between Member States and the Union based on the Treaties.
@ref Art 88(1) (src:1369)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the body is the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is the supervision or enforcement of Chapter V` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 88(1) the body has the power to supervise and enforce Chapter V` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such power
    ELSE IF NOT `the matter is the supervision or enforcement of Chapter V`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "to supervise and enforce Chapter V"; for another matter the sentence is silent
         ELSE IF `the body is the Commission`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commission shall have exclusive powers to supervise and enforce Chapter V"

@ref Art 88(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 88(1) the Commission must entrust the implementation of these tasks to the AI Office` MEANS
    IF `Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed

@ref Art 88(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 88 party` `Art 88 act`
`Art 88(1) the duty of the Commission to entrust the implementation of these tasks to the AI Office` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 88(1) the Commission must entrust the implementation of these tasks to the AI Office` `the date asked`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 88 the Commission`
        MUST `Art 88(1) entrust the implementation of the tasks of supervising and enforcing Chapter V to the AI Office`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- src:1370 | 2. Without prejudice to Article 75(3), market surveillance authorities may request the Commission to exercise the powers laid down in this Section, where that is necessary and proportionate to assist with the fulfilment of their tasks under this Regulation.
@ref Art 88(2) (src:1370)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the exercise of the powers is necessary and proportionate to assist with the fulfilment of the tasks of the market surveillance authority under this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 88(2) the market surveillance authority may request the Commission to exercise the powers laid down in this Section` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such power
    ELSE IF `the exercise of the powers is necessary and proportionate to assist with the fulfilment of the tasks of the market surveillance authority under this Regulation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "market surveillance authorities may request the Commission to exercise the powers laid down in this Section, where that is necessary and proportionate to assist with the fulfilment of their tasks" (a "where" gate on a "may": split site (ii), fork F-88-2)

§ `Article 89: monitoring actions`

-- src:1373 | 1. For the purpose of carrying out the tasks assigned to it under this Section, the AI Office may take the necessary actions to monitor the effective implementation and compliance with this Regulation by providers of general-purpose AI models, including their adherence to approved codes of practice.
@ref Art 89(1) (src:1373)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the monitoring concerns a provider of a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the actions are taken for the purpose of carrying out the tasks assigned to the AI Office under this Section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 89(1) the AI Office may take the necessary actions to monitor the effective implementation and compliance` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such power
    ELSE IF       `the monitoring concerns a provider of a general-purpose AI model`
              AND `the actions are taken for the purpose of carrying out the tasks assigned to the AI Office under this Section`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "for the purpose of carrying out the tasks assigned to it under this Section" and to monitor "providers of general-purpose AI models"; outside that the text neither gives nor refuses the power

-- src:1374 | 2. Downstream providers shall have the right to lodge a complaint alleging an infringement of this Regulation. A complaint shall be duly reasoned and indicate at least:
-- src:1375 | (a) the point of contact of the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned;
-- src:1376 | (b) a description of the relevant facts, the provisions of this Regulation concerned, and the reason why the downstream provider considers that the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned infringed this Regulation;
-- src:1377 | (c) any other information that the downstream provider that sent the request considers relevant, including, where appropriate, information gathered on its own initiative.
@ref Art 89(2) (src:1374-1377)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the person is a downstream provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complaint alleges an infringement of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 89(2) the downstream provider has the right to lodge a complaint alleging an infringement of this Regulation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such right
    ELSE IF       `the person is a downstream provider`
              AND `the complaint alleges an infringement of this Regulation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is given to "downstream providers" to "lodge a complaint alleging an infringement of this Regulation"; for another person or another complaint the text is silent (a right is counted with the grants: fork F-89-2)

-- "A complaint shall be duly reasoned and indicate at least": the points (a), (b) and (c).
-- Point (c) names information "that the downstream provider ... considers relevant": it is required only if there is any.
@ref Art 89(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the complaint is duly reasoned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complaint indicates the point of contact of the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complaint indicates a description of the relevant facts, the provisions of this Regulation concerned, and the reason why the downstream provider considers that the provider concerned infringed this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the downstream provider considers other information relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complaint indicates that other information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 89(2) the complaint is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is required
    ELSE IF       `the complaint is duly reasoned`
              AND `the complaint indicates the point of contact of the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned`
              AND `the complaint indicates a description of the relevant facts, the provisions of this Regulation concerned, and the reason why the downstream provider considers that the provider concerned infringed this Regulation`
              AND ((NOT `the downstream provider considers other information relevant`) OR `the complaint indicates that other information`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A complaint shall be duly reasoned and indicate at least" (a requirement of form with a floor, "at least": not met means the requirement is not met)

§ `Article 90: alerts of systemic risks by the scientific panel`

DECLARE `Art 90 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 90 the AI Office`

DECLARE `Art 90 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 90(2) inform the Board of any measure according to Articles 91 to 94`

-- src:1380 | 1. The scientific panel may provide a qualified alert to the AI Office where it has reason to suspect that:
-- src:1381 | (a) a general-purpose AI model poses concrete identifiable risk at Union level; or
-- src:1382 | (b) a general-purpose AI model meets the conditions referred to in Article 51.
@ref Art 90(1) (src:1380-1382)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the scientific panel has reason to suspect that a general-purpose AI model poses concrete identifiable risk at Union level` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scientific panel has reason to suspect that a general-purpose AI model meets the conditions referred to in Article 51` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 90(1) the scientific panel may provide a qualified alert to the AI Office` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such power
    ELSE IF       `the scientific panel has reason to suspect that a general-purpose AI model poses concrete identifiable risk at Union level`
               OR `the scientific panel has reason to suspect that a general-purpose AI model meets the conditions referred to in Article 51`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The scientific panel may provide a qualified alert to the AI Office where it has reason to suspect that: (a) ...; or (b) ..." (a "where" gate on a "may": split site (ii), fork F-90-1)

-- src:1383 | 2. Upon such qualified alert, the Commission, through the AI Office and after having informed the Board, may exercise the powers laid down in this Section for the purpose of assessing the matter. The AI Office shall inform the Board of any measure according to Articles 91 to 94.
@ref Art 90(2) (src:1383)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `a qualified alert has been provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has informed the Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 90(2) the Commission may exercise the powers laid down in this Section for the purpose of assessing the matter` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such power
    ELSE IF       `a qualified alert has been provided`
              AND `the Commission has informed the Board`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon such qualified alert, the Commission, through the AI Office and after having informed the Board, may exercise the powers laid down in this Section" (an "upon" and an "after" gate on a "may": split site (ii), fork F-90-2)

@ref Art 90(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office has taken a measure according to Articles 91 to 94` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 90(2) the AI Office must inform the Board of any measure according to Articles 91 to 94` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `the AI Office has taken a measure according to Articles 91 to 94`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to inform "of any measure according to Articles 91 to 94", which exists only once a measure is taken

@ref Art 90(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office has taken a measure according to Articles 91 to 94` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 90 party` `Art 90 act`
`Art 90(2) the duty of the AI Office to inform the Board of any measure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 90(2) the AI Office must inform the Board of any measure according to Articles 91 to 94` `the date asked` `the AI Office has taken a measure according to Articles 91 to 94`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 90 the AI Office`
        MUST `Art 90(2) inform the Board of any measure according to Articles 91 to 94`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- src:1384 | 3. A qualified alert shall be duly reasoned and indicate at least:
-- src:1385 | (a) the point of contact of the provider of the general-purpose AI model with systemic risk concerned;
-- src:1386 | (b) a description of the relevant facts and the reasons for the alert by the scientific panel;
-- src:1387 | (c) any other information that the scientific panel considers to be relevant, including, where appropriate, information gathered on its own initiative.
@ref Art 90(3) (src:1384-1387)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
