      `the qualified alert indicates the point of contact of the provider of the general-purpose AI model with systemic risk concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the qualified alert indicates a description of the relevant facts and the reasons for the alert by the scientific panel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scientific panel considers other information relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the qualified alert indicates that other information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 90(3) the qualified alert is duly reasoned and indicates at least the required points` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is required
    ELSE IF       `the qualified alert is duly reasoned`
              AND `the qualified alert indicates the point of contact of the provider of the general-purpose AI model with systemic risk concerned`
              AND `the qualified alert indicates a description of the relevant facts and the reasons for the alert by the scientific panel`
              AND ((NOT `the scientific panel considers other information relevant`) OR `the qualified alert indicates that other information`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A qualified alert shall be duly reasoned and indicate at least" (a requirement of form with a floor, "at least": not met means the requirement is not met)

§ `Article 91: power to request documentation and information`

DECLARE `Art 91 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 91 the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned`
    `Art 91 the person authorised to represent the provider`

DECLARE `Art 91 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 91(5) supply the information requested`

-- src:1390 | 1. The Commission may request the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned to provide the documentation drawn up by the provider in accordance with Articles 53 and 55, or any additional information that is necessary for the purpose of assessing compliance of the provider with this Regulation.
@ref Art 91(1) (src:1390)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the request is for the documentation drawn up by the provider in accordance with Articles 53 and 55` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is for additional information that is necessary for the purpose of assessing compliance of the provider with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 91(1) the Commission may request the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned to provide the documentation or information` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such power
    ELSE IF       `the request is for the documentation drawn up by the provider in accordance with Articles 53 and 55`
               OR `the request is for additional information that is necessary for the purpose of assessing compliance of the provider with this Regulation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant names the documentation drawn up under Articles 53 and 55 and "any additional information that is necessary for the purpose of assessing compliance"; a request for anything else is neither given nor refused

-- src:1391 | 2. Before sending the request for information, the AI Office may initiate a structured dialogue with the provider of the general-purpose AI model.
@ref Art 91(2) (src:1391)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office is about to send a request for information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 91(2) the AI Office may initiate a structured dialogue with the provider before sending the request for information` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such power
    ELSE IF `the AI Office is about to send a request for information`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for "before sending the request for information"; once the request is sent the sentence is silent

-- src:1392 | 3. Upon a duly substantiated request from the scientific panel, the Commission may issue a request for information to a provider of a general-purpose AI model, where the access to information is necessary and proportionate for the fulfilment of the tasks of the scientific panel under Article 68(2).
@ref Art 91(3) (src:1392)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the scientific panel has made a duly substantiated request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the access to information is necessary and proportionate for the fulfilment of the tasks of the scientific panel under Article 68(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 91(3) the Commission may issue a request for information to the provider on the request of the scientific panel` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such power
    ELSE IF       `the scientific panel has made a duly substantiated request`
              AND `the access to information is necessary and proportionate for the fulfilment of the tasks of the scientific panel under Article 68(2)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon a duly substantiated request from the scientific panel, the Commission may issue a request for information to a provider of a general-purpose AI model, where the access to information is necessary and proportionate" (an "upon" and a "where" gate on a "may": split site (ii), fork F-91-3)

-- src:1393 | 4. The request for information shall state the legal basis and the purpose of the request, specify what information is required, set a period within which the information is to be provided, and indicate the fines provided for in Article 101 for supplying incorrect, incomplete or misleading information.
@ref Art 91(4) (src:1393)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the request states the legal basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request states the purpose of the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request specifies what information is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request sets a period within which the information is to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request indicates the fines provided for in Article 101 for supplying incorrect, incomplete or misleading information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 91(4) the request for information has the required content` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is required
    ELSE IF       `the request states the legal basis`
              AND `the request states the purpose of the request`
              AND `the request specifies what information is required`
              AND `the request sets a period within which the information is to be provided`
              AND `the request indicates the fines provided for in Article 101 for supplying incorrect, incomplete or misleading information`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The request for information shall state the legal basis and the purpose of the request, specify what information is required, set a period within which the information is to be provided, and indicate the fines" (a requirement of form: a missing item means the request lacks the required content)

-- The provider's duty to supply the information requested, within the period the request sets (paragraph 4).
-- src:1394 | 5. The provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned, or its representative shall supply the information requested. In the case of legal persons, companies or firms, or where the provider has no legal personality, the persons authorised to represent them by law or by their statutes, shall supply the information requested on behalf of the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned. Lawyers duly authorised to act may supply information on behalf of their clients. The clients shall nevertheless remain fully responsible if the information supplied is incomplete, incorrect or misleading.
@ref Art 91(5) (src:1394)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission has requested the information under Article 91` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 91(5) the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned must supply the information requested` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `the Commission has requested the information under Article 91`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to supply "the information requested", which exists only once a request is made

@ref Art 91(5)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission has requested the information under Article 91` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the period set in the request began` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period set in the request ends` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 91 party` `Art 91 act`
`Art 91(5) the duty of the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned to supply the information requested` MEANS
    IF       `Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`
         AND `the Commission has requested the information under Article 91`
    THEN PARTY `Art 91 the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned`
         MUST `Art 91(5) supply the information requested`
         WITHIN (Day `the day on which the period set in the request ends`) MINUS (Day `the day on which the period set in the request began`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Art 91 the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned` BECAUSE "the information requested was not supplied within the period the request set under Article 91(4)"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

@ref Art 91(5)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission has requested the information under Article 91` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider is a legal person, a company or a firm, or has no legal personality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 91(5) the persons authorised to represent the provider must supply the information requested on its behalf` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF       `the Commission has requested the information under Article 91`
              AND `the provider is a legal person, a company or a firm, or has no legal personality`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "legal persons, companies or firms, or where the provider has no legal personality"; for a natural person with legal personality it is silent

@ref Art 91(5)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the lawyer is duly authorised to act for the client` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 91(5) a lawyer may supply information on behalf of the client` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such permission
    ELSE IF `the lawyer is duly authorised to act for the client`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to "lawyers duly authorised to act"; for another person it is silent

@ref Art 91(5)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the information was supplied on behalf of the provider by a duly authorised lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information supplied is incomplete, incorrect or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 91(5) the client remains fully responsible` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `the information was supplied on behalf of the provider by a duly authorised lawyer`
         THEN IF `the information supplied is incomplete, incorrect or misleading`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The clients shall nevertheless remain fully responsible if the information supplied is incomplete, incorrect or misleading" (an "if" condition that is not met: the sentence makes the client responsible for incomplete, incorrect or misleading information only)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "their clients", the clients of a lawyer who supplied the information

§ `Article 92: power to conduct evaluations`

DECLARE `Art 92 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 92 the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned`
    `Art 92 the person authorised to represent the provider`
    `Art 92 the Commission`

DECLARE `Art 92 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 92(5) supply the access requested`
    `Art 92(6) adopt implementing acts setting out the detailed arrangements and the conditions for the evaluations`

-- src:1397 | 1. The AI Office, after consulting the Board, may conduct evaluations of the general-purpose AI model concerned:
-- src:1398 | (a) to assess compliance of the provider with obligations under this Regulation, where the information gathered pursuant to Article 91 is insufficient; or
-- src:1399 | (b) to investigate systemic risks at Union level of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk, in particular following a qualified alert from the scientific panel in accordance with Article 90(1), point (a).
@ref Art 92(1) (src:1397-1399)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office has consulted the Board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to assess compliance of the provider with obligations under this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information gathered pursuant to Article 91 is insufficient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to investigate systemic risks at Union level of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 92(1) the AI Office may conduct an evaluation of the general-purpose AI model concerned` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application; before that the Regulation gives no such power
    ELSE IF NOT `the AI Office has consulted the Board`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The AI Office, after consulting the Board, may conduct evaluations" (an "after consulting" gate on a "may": split site (ii), fork F-92-1a)
         ELSE IF `the purpose is to investigate systemic risks at Union level of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk`
              THEN JUST TRUE  -- point (b): the words "in particular following a qualified alert" are an example, not a condition
              ELSE IF `the purpose is to assess compliance of the provider with obligations under this Regulation`
                   THEN IF `the information gathered pursuant to Article 91 is insufficient`
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) to assess compliance of the provider with obligations under this Regulation, where the information gathered pursuant to Article 91 is insufficient" (a "where" gate on a "may": split site (ii), fork F-92-1b)
                   ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the grant names two purposes, (a) and (b), and does not say "only"

